@startuml mbtb_late_recover
title Timed uBTB -> mBTB override and the required O3 recovery boundary
autonumber
hide footbox
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam maxMessageSize 95

participant "CustomBPU : IBPU" as BPU
participant "uBTB" as UBTB
participant "mBTB pipeline" as MBTB
participant "ResponseQueue / ledger" as Queue
participant "Gem5BpuBridge" as Bridge
participant "FTQ" as FTQ
participant "Fetch / BlockFetchEngine" as Fetch
participant "O3OverrideHook" as Hook
participant "Commit / recovery arbitration" as Commit

legend left
  [E] Existing gem5 method or signal
  [N] Proposed IBPU / bridge integration
  [A] Illustrative internal operation, not an existing method
  This is a design contract, not an implemented gem5 call path.
endlegend

== One dynamic query and two result times ==
BPU -> BPU : [A] checkpoint history for key=(tid,id,generation)
BPU -> MBTB : [A] accept slow query(key, queryPC, history), at t_issue
BPU -> UBTB : [A] accept fast query for the same dynamic boundary
UBTB --> BPU : [A] fast predicted blocks, ready at t_fast
BPU -> Queue : [A] append fast target; advance speculative uBTB path
opt FTQ slot and insertion budget available
    Bridge -> BPU : [N] canSupply(now); peekFetchTarget()
    BPU --> Bridge : [N] stable fast payload when ready
    Bridge -> Bridge : [N] makeFT(payload)
    Bridge -> FTQ : [N] reuse insert(tid, ft)
    Bridge -> BPU : [N] acceptFetchTarget(key, now)
end
loop Later cycles before the slow result/override becomes ready
    BPU -> UBTB : [A] predict next dynamic query on the fast path
    BPU -> Queue : [A] record readyCycle and speculative dependencies
    opt A fast-path target was admitted
        Fetch -> FTQ : [E] readHead(tid)
        FTQ --> Fetch : [E] published fast-path target
    end
end
MBTB --> BPU : [A] slow result(key), ready at t_issue + n
BPU -> BPU : [A] compare CFI sequence, direction, targets, span and nextQueryPC
alt Same live prediction
    BPU -> Queue : [A] mark slow result checked; no redirect
else Different live prediction
    BPU -> Queue : [A] enqueue OverrideEvent(eventId, cut, \
replacementSuffix,\nreadyCycle=t_issue+n+redirectLatency)
end
note over BPU, Queue
  Host lookahead may compute m results first using isolated checkpoints.
  It must not expose the slow result before its simulated readyCycle,
  advance live history twice, or add n again after detecting disagreement.
  Issue interval and latency are separate. No FTQ slot is required to
  advance an already accepted pipeline result or service a control event.
  Wrong-path duration is measured from t_fast to effective redirect;
  FTQ pressure and O3 recovery delay can change how far that path advances.
end note

== Bridge services controls even when FTQ is full ==
Bridge -> Bridge : [N] forwardFeedback(timeBuffer): process existing \
recovery first
Bridge -> BPU : [N] peekOverride(now)
BPU --> Bridge : [N] ready OverrideEvent, stable until acknowledged
Bridge -> Bridge : [A] validate key/cut against live ledger, age and actual \
resolution
alt Cut was canceled, superseded, retired or already authoritatively resolved
    Bridge -> BPU : [N] ackOverride(eventId), only after recording discard
    note right of Bridge
      ack means this event has been handled, not that a redirect succeeded.
      PC equality is insufficient; reject stale dynamic identities.
    end note
else Event is live
    Bridge -> Bridge : [N] applyOverride(event)
    alt Affected suffix exists only in the BPU response queue
        Bridge -> BPU : [N] onRecovery(cause=PredictorOverride, cut, \
restartPC,\nresolvedOutcome absent)
        BPU -> Queue : [A] rollback history at cut; invalidate younger \
data/control\ninstall corrected suffix and nextQueryPC
        Bridge -> BPU : [N] ackOverride(eventId), after application
    else Affected suffix is in FTQ/assembly; no affected DynInst was built
        Bridge -> FTQ : [N] squashAfter(cut); replaceSuffix(cut, blocks)
        Bridge -> Fetch : [N] invalidateYounger(cut); repair cursor at \
restartPC
        Bridge -> BPU : [N] onRecovery(cause=PredictorOverride, cut, \
restartPC,\nresolvedOutcome absent)
        BPU -> Queue : [A] rollback and replace speculative suffix
        Bridge -> BPU : [N] ackOverride(eventId), after application
    else Affected DynInsts exist only in Fetch's local fetchQueue
        Bridge -> Fetch : [A] selectively remove affected local DynInsts\n\
repair source prediction and decoder/cursor consistently
        Bridge -> FTQ : [N] squashAfter(cut); replaceSuffix(cut, blocks)
        Bridge -> Fetch : [N] invalidateYounger(cut)
        Bridge -> BPU : [N] onRecovery(cause=PredictorOverride, cut, \
restartPC,\nresolvedOutcome absent)
        Bridge -> BPU : [N] ackOverride(eventId), after all local repair is \
applied
        note right of Fetch
          This selective Fetch repair is NEW. Existing doSquash()
          clears all local fetchQueue entries, including a valid prefix.
          Check whether the source branch prediction can be changed safely;
          an earlier source that left Fetch requires the O3 path below.
        end note
    else Affected instruction OR source prediction has left Fetch
        Bridge -> Hook : [N] requestSquash(cut, restartPC)
        Hook -> Hook : [A] retain pending eventId + cut + prediction generation
        Hook --> Bridge : [A] request queued; not yet accepted/applied
        note over Bridge, Commit
          New asynchronous protocol: freeze affected publication/consumption
          until accepted or superseded, keep event pending, and do not ack yet.
          The current class exposes request/arbitrate; it also needs a precise
          completion status or callback before implementation can be correct.
        end note
        ... O3 recovery arbitration point ...
        Hook -> Hook : [N] arbitrateWithExistingRecovery()
        Hook -> Commit : [A] propose live predictor-only cut with source \
identity
        Commit -> Commit : [A] arbitrate against actual outcomes, traps and \
older cuts\nrecheck source resolution and youngest valid boundary
        alt Existing authoritative recovery supersedes the request
            Commit --> Hook : [A] canceled/superseded completion
            Hook --> Bridge : [A] report final disposition
            Bridge -> BPU : [N] ackOverride(eventId), after discard is recorded
        else Predictor-only recovery accepted
            Commit -> Commit : [A] start suffix squash with explicit \
predictor cause\npreserve/update source prediction safely, or replay source
            Commit --> Fetch : [N] delayed recovery broadcast with predictor \
cause\nreset affected stream and dynamic instructions
            Commit --> Bridge : [N] delayed applied recovery with matching \
eventId
            Bridge -> FTQ : [N] squashAfter(cut); replaceSuffix(cut, blocks)
            Bridge -> Fetch : [N] invalidateYounger(cut)
            Bridge -> BPU : [N] onRecovery(cause=PredictorOverride, cut, \
restartPC,\nresolvedOutcome absent)
            BPU -> Queue : [A] rollback younger histories and pending \
results\nadvance from the installed slow prediction
            Bridge -> BPU : [N] ackOverride(eventId), after coordinated \
application
        end
    end
end
note over BPU, Commit
  Preserve unaffected prefix requests and history. Reject canceled replies
  by RequestTag; cancel younger override events as well as data results.
  A prediction may span several blocks: cut is key + block/CFI/instSeq,
  not just an FTSeqNum or address interval.
  Updating the source DynInst prediction must match ledger/history state.
  If replaying the source is chosen, includeBoundary and restart PC change
  accordingly; replay is not a free timing-equivalent implementation.
end note
note over Bridge, Commit
  Existing anchors: BAC::checkAndUpdateBPUSignals(), bac.cc:290;
  Fetch::doSquash()/bacResteer(), fetch.cc:710/762;
  IEW::squashDueToBranch(), iew.cc:473; Commit::commit(), commit.cc:755.
  None accepts predictor-only recovery today. Extending the arbitration
  and broadcast is required; calling bacResteer() alone cannot remove
  wrong-path Decode/Rename/ROB/IQ/LSQ instructions.
  Do not encode a slow prediction as mispredictInst + actual branchTaken.
end note
@enduml
